NegroniMetal change to metal2vulkan 720ef1ce (+ the ios-flame bridge patches), applied by scripts/metal/fetch-sources.sh:
no-copy buffers (newBufferWithBytesNoCopy:, IOSurface textures) on a device whose host-pointer imports allow only
host-visible types without HOST_COHERENT (Turnip on Darwin/RedwoodGPU: HOST_CACHED, docs/gpu-abi.md section 6).
- memory.rs: Memory::import_host falls back to such types (cached first) where no coherent type is allowed; before
  this the import was refused as Unsupported { HostMemory, NotRepresentable } (no memory type of the class).
- command_buffer/mod.rs: as a command buffer completes, before its status and its completed handlers, it calls
  vkInvalidateMappedMemoryRanges over each such import its commands used (no-copy buffers, buffers under textures,
  no-copy heaps). Turnip does dc civac by the caller's pointer. The CPU-to-GPU direction is the kernel's: it cleans
  CPU-written pages of 0x49 and 0x7e imports at each submission that lists them (gpu-abi.md section 6 rule 1).
- buffer.rs: HostPages::import_range (memory, offset, size of the import) for that call.

